course: dictionary
lesson: 8679
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning the writer means. Seed is a good example. «Seeds must travel away from their parent, so the young plants do not compete with it for light and water.» Here a seed is the small hard part of a plant that can grow into a new plant.
explain: «The seed of an idea» is where an idea starts. The word seed is not about a plant at all. Always ask: which meaning fits the sentence? Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Seed can also be a doing word. «To seed a field is to plant seeds in it.» Seed, seeds, seeded and seeding all come from one word, so when you meet seeded or seeding, look for the action in the sentence.
explain: In sport, a seed is a strong player placed so that the top players do not meet early in a tournament. The clues are the words around it, such as tournament and placed. Once you spot those clues, the right meaning is easy to find.
fact: A seed is the small hard part of a plant that can grow into a new plant.
fact: Seeds are also the small pips inside fruit, like apple seeds or melon seeds.
fact: «Seeds must travel away from their parent» so that young plants do not compete with it for light and water.
fact: «A hamster can stuff its cheeks so full of seeds that its head looks twice as wide.»
fact: A seed needs water, warmth and air to germinate, which means to start to grow.
exercise: «The seed of an idea grew into a plan.» What does seed mean here? | A strong player in a game | A small hard part of a plant | To plant seeds in a field | *Where an idea starts
exercise: «To seed a field is to plant seeds in it.» What kind of word is seed in this sentence? | A word for a player in a tournament | A naming word for a fruit pip | *A doing word, meaning to put seeds into the ground | A word for an idea
exercise: Ella says, «Melon seeds are the pips inside the fruit.» What does seeds mean here? | *The small pips inside fruit | Strong players placed in a tournament | The start of an idea | Plants that grow in rows
test: «Dandelion seeds fly on little parachutes.» What does seeds mean in this sentence? | Where an idea begins | A strong player in a tournament | The pips inside a melon | *The small hard parts of a plant that can grow into a new plant
test: Jayden reads, «The coach seeded the best players so they did not meet early.» What does seeded mean here? | Planted in the ground | Sprouted from a pip | *Placed as a strong player so top players do not meet early | Gave an idea to a team
exam: Rangers study droppings and find «seeds» inside fox droppings. What does seed mean here, and which words around it helped you decide? | A strong player in a tournament; the word droppings tells me it is a sport | The start of an idea; the word study tells me it is about thinking | A doing word; the word fox tells me it is an action | *The small hard parts of a plant that can grow into a new plant; the words fox droppings and find helped me decide
